## Prerequisites

- CMake 3.15 or higher
- A C++17 (or higher) compatible compiler

## Build Steps

1. Configure the project:
```bash
cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE={{ build_type }}
```

2. Build the project:
```bash
cmake --build build --config {{ build_type }}
```

3. {% if project_type == "executable" %}Run the executable:
```bash
./build/{{ project_slug }}
```{% else %}Use the library:
The library will be built in `build/lib/` (or `build/` on Windows) and can be linked against other projects.{% endif %}

### Build Types

Available build types:
- `Debug`: Debug build with no optimizations
- `Release`: Optimized release build
- `RelWithDebInfo`: Release build with debug information

## Testing

{% if include_tests %}
This project uses [Catch2](https://github.com/catchorg/Catch2) for testing.

### Running Tests

Build and run tests:
```bash
cmake --build build --target test
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

Or run the test executable directly:
```bash
./build/tests
```

### Test Structure

- Test files are located in the `tests/` directory
- The main test executable is `tests/test_main.cpp`
- Tests use Catch2's BDD-style macros for readable test cases

{% else %}
Testing is not enabled for this project. To enable testing, regenerate the project with `include_tests=true`.
{% endif %}

## Usage

{% if project_type == "library" %}
### Integration with CMake

Add this project to your CMake file:

```cmake
find_package({{ project_name }} REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(your_target {{ project_name }}::{{ project_name }})
```

### API Reference

```cpp
#include "{{ project_slug }}/{{ project_slug }}.hpp"

// Basic usage
int result = {{ project_slug }}::add(2, 3);
```

{% else %}
### Running the Application

After building, run the executable:
```bash
./build/{{ project_slug }}
```
{% endif %}

